<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40420" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rāpum</span></b> , i, n.
		akin to Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥάφη,
		ῥαφάνη</span> (collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rāpa</span></b> , ae, f., <i><span class="en">Col. 11, 3,
		16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 176</span></i>; <i><span class="en">177</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a turnip</i>, <i>rape</i>: Brassica rapa, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 59, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 2,
				10, 22 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 13, 33, § 125</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flung at one as an insult,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Vesp. 4</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A knob</i> or <i>lump</i> formed by
			the roots of a tree: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">magnarum arborum truncos cum rapo suo
					transtulit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 86, 17</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 86, 18</span></i>.</div>
